Z||000000||dennis_6||11-14-2001||07:55 PM||||Is there anyway to repair a bad case of clear coat peeling without have the car repainted?  Also how do you do those inverted question marks?  <P>can i pit nitris in my  92 Fard Excart, it haz a 1,9l injun with lifer rattle, but i now iz fas cuz I can sqeel tirs if I putz my car in nutral and stomp th gaz and then shif in driv.  Just a little fun I can't spell either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Kasdan||11-14-2001||09:11 PM||||I know not of the inverted question marks you speak of.<BR>¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿¿<BR>OK so maybe i do<BR>alt+111784.<BR>As to your other question, its beyond me.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sootah||11-14-2001||09:15 PM||||¿ ALT+168 is easier. Keep in mind you have to use the # pad for these, the number row above the letters will not work.<P>¿ = ALT+168<BR>¡ = ALT+173<BR>½ = ALT+171<BR>¼ = ALT+172<BR>º = ALT+167<P>º¿º <B><I>-Sootah</B></I><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">       <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>85 GT</A> - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>86 SE</A> (Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sootah||11-14-2001||09:18 PM||||Wet sand, wash, polishing compound, wash, wax, wash, stand back and admire your work.<P><B>DISCLAIMER</B>: Never done this myself, but it should work. Just be careful not to sand all the way through the paint. When wet sanding just sand lightly till the water becomes paint colored AND NO MORE.<P><B>PEACE <I>-Sootah</B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JB||11-14-2001||09:53 PM||||I regret to inform you that your clearcoat is officialy D.O.A.!!!!  I Manage a Body Shop so believe me when I tell you that If your clearcoat is peeling, the only way to fix it is to repaint it.  Sorry to be the bearer of bad news!    Computers,..... I dont know much about!||||reg||1
Z||000005||dennis_6||11-15-2001||02:38 AM||||¿¿¿Cool you learn something new everyday <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks everyone.  Guess I will just have to get my door and trunk lid painted.<BR>Suprised no one knew about nitrous on an Escort.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-15-2001||05:35 AM||||Hi JB, just to say nice to see some more body shop guys in here. Reason you cant just sand and polish it is that basecoat colors are flat (completly dull) and get their gloss from the clearcoat. It would be like trying to shine up a flat black hood-wont work. May look better than peeling, but wont shine.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfixit58||11-15-2001||09:56 AM||||What about clear coat that's NOT peeling? I've got some black fungus-looking stuff that appears to be growing UNDER my clear coat. Can I lightly sand with 1000 grit down to the paint then just re-clear?<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||11-15-2001||12:51 PM||||may get away with it for temporary. Clearcoat normally has to be applied within 12 hours or so of a base color to adhere to it. I let my bases dry for 1 hour. Clear over old base like your talking may last a year, may only last a week-no way to tell.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JB||11-15-2001||09:25 PM||||Thanks for the welcome Roger.  And for the record, I agree with your opinion on the "fungus" question.||||reg||1
